Before I describe this particular ascension I'd like to mention that
I'm an action player in addition to being a gambler(comes from playing
way too much poker) so I've always skipped a lot of content and played
fast(often resulting in early deaths). A speed ascension seemed like a
good way to go after 15ish ascensions and ~2 years of Nethacking. A few
poor attempts at chaotic elven wizards with DfV-fantasies proved
worthless and I kept dying at the castle, thus I tried to complete the
gnomish mines first, then do soko if I was still missing boh/"oR. This
tactic has worked out fine for me; turning out many decently fast but
somewhat unimpressive ascensions:

(The last 8)
17347(mon), 21333(wiz), 18357(wiz), 23301(mon), 23907(wiz), 17096(mon),
18593(wiz), 18344(bar) turns...

As you can see, I don't make a habit of finding /oWishing except at the
castle, where they're usually 0:1 and heiniously cursed. I've found
that once I complete VotD, the rest of the game is easy for me. I've
actually never died after VotD, except for a choking accident and
#quitting.

So I figured I'd do another speed ascension and really try hard to get
a good turn count this time around. Although this game was lined with
minor mistakes, I had a blast (plus it only took like 3 1/2 hours from
start to finish:P) Anyway!

Chaggog the neutral monk started out with the protection spellbook and
u?oGeno. Quickly abandoned the pet and found an altar(two actually,
cha+neu) at dlvl2. An early shop provided speed boots(hooray), some
gauntlets and a cloak of invis(useless). I proceeded quickly down to
the mine town. The altar there turned out be neutral as well. The
stores were pretty crappy, but I did pick up a stethoscope, a key and a
blindfold. Decided to head down to the bottom and pick up the
luckstone. This turned out to be a good idea as I found a magic lamp,
pick-axe and a boh somewhere along the way. I saw a baby silver dragon
and found a poly trap with manual searching. I ran up to the main
dungeon and started digging down. Each level was checked only with a
blindfold+telepathy gained from a floating eye. Further down Chaggog's
ghost guarded an absolutely worthless bones pile(I have no idea).
Picked up maybe 6 random scrolls and some cursed food there. An armor
shop gave me a helm of telepathy and some jumping boots, I put both on
and the jumping began. Dug down at the Oracle and ended up two levels
down, thought about doing soko and decided to keep digging. In
retrospect I should've done the first level for a wand, scrolls and the
"eye's tele. Oh well.

Found medusa at dlvl27, titan version.. oops. Wrote Elbereth with my
fingers and dug down. Found the upstairs and killed Medusa for some
obscure reason.

At turn 5000 or so I arrived at the castle, the level just above it had
given me a harp;) Engraved the E word with a /oFire and did the
drawbridge trick to clear the first part of the castle. Wand was at the
upper-west part of the level.

Okay, wishing time...
First wish went for 2b?oC(got them). Zapped again- Nothing happens.
...great... recharged.
"eye
+oPoly
helm of brilliance+3(got +0:((()
then I sat down and thought about what marker I needed, thought maybe
an unholy one might be better but decided to wait a little while. This
turned out to be an excellent choice(pats himself on the back) as the
castle throne gave old Chaggog a wish - holy magic marker.

Did some polymorphing for a bunch of spells and a ring of free action.
Cleared the castle guards and got a ton of food, emptied the food
supply near the dragons too (I actually only had 2 K-rations left when
I offered the amulet, gulp!). Votd gave me some polyfodder and a few
levels, gated back to mine town and reached level 15 or so, did some
polypiling and got the important spells and =oC, =oLev and =oFA. Also
enchanted my junk and donated gold for 4 points of protection.

With the glorious stats of 100ish hp and -12ac I was ready for the
ascension run! Dug through the levels of Gehennom and found Vlad quick.
Continued down and killed the Wizard then the Sanctum. After obtaining
the amulet I looked through my boh and noticed that I had only one
potion of holy water and zero blank scrolls, oops? The holy water
wasn't a big problem, I had the spell of remove curse, the paper loss
sucked though. Ah well, End game is a piece of cake. Wizard came back a
few times and my /oDeath ran out of charges, recharged it once and then
I ran out of ?oC, blergh... Had some trouble going up with -15ish ac so
I put on a (orange or something)DSM for some extra ac. Needless to say
the way up took many, many turns. This would've been a 10k turn
ascension if I didn't suck so bad. Having not found a single !oBooze
but 10+ tripe rations I felt it was going to be an easy ascension.
Climed up at dlvl1 and ate about 8 tripes without getting confused
once. Eventually it worked and I proceeded through earth without
problems. Air absolutely stunk but I won after a few close calls. Fire-
no ways to confuse myself. Hmm. I just wandered around for a while and
a happy Archon showed to party with me. He summoned some nasties but I
found the ^. Water was easy since I had geno'd ; previously. I arrived
at the Astral plane with 1 !FH and my last /oTele at 3 charges :P  Left
altar had death and some junk but I just jumped past them. Danced
around with some Angels and priests and finally jumped onto the _ after
13858 moves. Oh well, not all that great but not bad either. A new
record for me anyway.

Feedback or tips are welcome, thanks for reading.



